{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986907-paradox-and-wisdom-branding","id":986907,"title":"Paradox and Wisdom Branding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T13:06:38-07:00","id":986907,"title":"Paradox and Wisdom Branding","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Thought it would be cute to bring back Branding from first edition, which I was fond of:</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">New Paradox Condition - Branding:</span></span></span></b><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The Branded Condition gives mage a strange new feature as their pattern absorbs a spell's paradox. Each feature costs a certain number of paradox successes, see below:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Successes</span></span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Brand</span></span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Description</span></span></b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Witch Mark</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">A blemish or mark, or a minor effect like a pallor, luminous motes in the eyes, radiating heat, or the like.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Disfigurement</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">A significant, often unnatural effect, like metallic skin, animal pupils, a weird tenor to her voice. -1 Social rolls with Sleepers who perceive it, except Intimidation.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Bestial Feature</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Claws, fangs, horns, tail, fur, scales. -3 Social rolls with Sleepers who perceive the feature, except Intimidation.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Inhuman Feature</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Clearly demonic or supernatural features, like glowing eyes, a forked tail, a cloud of flies, a miasma that makes plants wither, a pall of smoke. Their presence may inflict breaking points on Sleepers who perceive them and suffer a -5 penalty to Social rolls against </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><i>anyone,</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> aside from Intimidation.</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><u>Resolution</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">: The mage accepts the feature, raising it one step in duration (a year for Enlightened Wisdom), scouring your own pattern for 1 lethal, or allowing the Condition to lapse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <hr /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Also wanted to expand it a little bit, so here's another optional idea:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Wisdom Branding:</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Instead of losing a dot of Wisdom, a mage may accept a Brand. This is functionally similar to the Branding Condition, but is a permanent part of the mage\u2019s pattern, and instead of being essentially random based on the spell, it follows a theme, such as a mage who is slowly turning into a phoenix, a demonic or angelic figure, a wolf for a Wolf-blooded mage, or some other theme related to who they are.<br /> In order to remove the Brand, the mage has to raise her Wisdom above where it was when she received the Brand (or, for Wisdom 10, take an Obsession to remove it.)</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:17:26-07:00","id":986948,"title":"","content":"An interesting notion this triggered: <br /> <br /> Paradox brands are something that a mage can develop that improves their ability to contain Paradox. Basically, brands are seals of various levels that contain paradox within a pattern, even should their wisdom prove insufficient to the task. They are developed by the effort of containing and then falling, so they are looked on as both a badge of distinction and failure by many. They are normally linked to a path or arcana, but other forms exist. <br /> <br /> They generally have a non-metaphysical use and a drawback, as well, all tied to the paradox absorbed.<br /> <br /> The classical witch's nipple, for example, is a Path Mark for Thyrsus Which helps contain paradox for life and spirit effects, but also can be used to suckle any mammal or spirit. (Classical sense: it produces the fed creature's natural form of milk, if any.) This is true regardless of any other physical realities. The nipple is similar to a fetish with a paradox pool equal to the mages permanent Composure. <br /> <br /> Attempts to drain it of essence provoke a Paradox roll. Success in draining out of essence reduces the paradox stored, and increases the paradox rolls of everyone present as if they had cast a vulgar spell. Instead of essence, the recipient of the essence gains a success on their Paradox roll per essence drawn, if they cast this effect, or they must contain one as if they did otherwise. They only need to contend with the successes sent their way, in that case, and not roll their pool.<br /> <br /> When the paradox it's drained, the Mark normally fades.<br /> <br /> <br /> Accanthus tend to pick up strange bans called Paradoxical Gaesi. This form of Geas uses Paradox as the number of times disaster will strike should the mage fail to maintain the stricture. The effect duplicated is Sworn Oaths, but the mage doesn't choose the terms. Fate can easily read these but altering them is dangerous. <br /> <br /> The advantage is that the mage may channel their paradoxical geas to use the better of their stored paradox or the effect's normal number of hits by spending one stored point of Paradox. This only works to hex others, however, not to bless or protect them.<br /> <br /> Attempts to alter the gaes always provoke paradox rolls. A successful casting works as normal, otherwise, but the caster gains a new paradoxical gaes of some sort with a paradox point in it and the original gaes returns reduced only by one, and the effects of the alternating cannot be lasting.<br /> <br /> Violating the gaes releases the stored paradox along with rolling the mage's Paradox die pool. <br /> <br /> Completely off the top of my head, here, but that sounds neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  Spelling 10-13-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T20:46:56-07:00","id":987084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/986907-paradox-and-wisdom-branding?p=986948#post986948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The classical witch's nipple, for example, is a Path Mark for Thyrsus Which helps contain paradox for life and spirit effects, but also can be used to suckle any mammal or spirit. (Classical sense: it produces the fed creature's natural form of milk, if any.) This is true regardless of any other physical realities. The nipple is similar to a fetish with a paradox pool equal to the mages permanent Composure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That specific thing is already a Werewolf Tell that can feed spirits essence, though it's a perfectly viable option sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-15-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}